Maintain this architecture.

## Architecture principles

### Canonical data
The JSON persistent store remains the canonical source of truth for the prototype.

All financial records, commitments, transaction records, investigation cases, user confirmations, evidence and audit information must be saved through a reliable persistence path.

### Neo4j
Neo4j remains a real graph-based relationship and intelligence layer.

It must not become the sole canonical store of financial records.

Graph synchronization should remain a separately tracked operation. A graph sync failure must not cause the application to pretend that canonical persistence failed, nor should successful canonical persistence be represented as a fully synchronized graph when it is not.

### Sarvam AI
Preserve the actual Sarvam integrations and existing supported use cases.

AI may assist with language processing, translation, explanation, extraction and user-facing understanding, but must not independently:

- Confirm a merchant.
- Declare a mandate valid.
- Declare an actual debit authorized.
- Determine legal liability.
- Mark a commitment as verified.
- Claim that a cancellation was successful.
- Reconcile a financial transaction without deterministic supporting records.

### Deterministic financial engine
Financial calculations, amount matching, recurrence detection, mandate matching, transaction classification, evidence status, confidence classifications and reconciliation outcomes must remain deterministic.

AI output must be clearly distinguishable from verified financial information.

